{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he shall take off his garments.</b> This is not an obligation but derech eretz — that he not soil, while removing the ashes, the garments in which he regularly serves. With the garments in which he cooked a pot for his master, let him not pour a cup for his master. Therefore he puts on lesser garments than them (Sifra)." "<b>And he shall remove the ashes.</b> The accumulation on the hearth — when it is large and there is no room for the arrangement of wood, he removes it from there. And this is not an obligation every day, but the terumah is an obligation every day (Tamid 28)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:09.633592896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}